            <ArticleTitle>Late-onset post-diskectomy tuberculosis at the same operated lumbar level: case report and review of literature.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>S226-32</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1007/s00586-010-1420-z</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Late post-diskectomy tuberculous spondylodiskitis at the operated level is an extremely rare phenomenon. We describe a unique case of a same level tuberculous spondylodiskitis with pus drainage from the operative scar 8 years after simple L4/L5 diskectomy and review the relevant literature. The therapeutic management and possible pathogenic mechanisms are discussed as well.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
